				<div class="banner">
					<h2><span class="wsite-text wsite-headline">
	Even though how prepared you are for an earthquake, it is no surprise that injuries are to be expected.
</span></h2>
					<p><span class="wsite-text wsite-headline-paragraph">
	Do not add insult to injury!! Here are common injuries that may occur during an earthquake and the necessary first aid techniques to treat them.
</span></p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div><!-- banner-wrap -->

		<div class="main-wrap">
			<div class="container">
				<div id="wsite-content" class="wsite-elements wsite-not-footer">
	<div class="paragraph">Here is a flowchart to quickly guide you on different first aid procedures. If the injury of a person is not included in the ones mentioned in this web site, give necessary treatments needed to address that different injury.</div>

<div><div class="wsite-image wsite-image-border-none " style="padding-top:10px;padding-bottom:10px;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;text-align:center">
<a>
<img src="/uploads/4/0/3/9/40390011/14087528-543908735809472-390209020-o_orig.jpg" alt="Picture" style="width:auto;max-width:100%" />
</a>
<div style="display:block;font-size:90%"></div>
</div></div>

<h2 class="wsite-content-title">FIRST AID OF COMMON INJURIES AFTER AN EARTHQUAKE:</h2>

<div class="paragraph">- Open wounds:<br />1. Disinfect your hands with alcohol or wash them.<br />2. Gently apply pressure with a bandage or clean cloth and elevate wound.<br />3. Wash the wound in clean water and apply a small amount of antibiotic cream.<br />4. Cover the wound with bandage or clean cloth.<br /><br />&#8203;- Bruises:<br />1. Elevate the bruised area.<br />2. Apply pressure with an ice pack in damped cloth.<br />3. Rest the bruised area as much as possible.<br /><br />- Burns:<br />1. Run the burn over cool water (not cold!) until the pain eases.<br />2. Apply moisturizer or gel to reduce pain and relieve the burned area.<br />&#8203;3. Give necessary treatments.<br /></div>
</div>

			</div>
		</div><!-- main-wrap -->
